    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `GOLD` membership tier following the existing `namesakeCount` pattern \u2014 a create-time count snapshot persisted on the entity and read back by the DTO mapper.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `householdMemberCount` field (`@Column(name = \"household_member_count\")`) with getter/setter, mirroring `namesakeCount`.\n\n2. **Schema (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`)** \u2014 added the `household_member_count` column to the `owners` table in all four dialects (tests use `hsqldb`; the others kept in sync).\n\n3. **`AssignHouseholdSize.java`** (new function) \u2014 computes the household size *after* this create: existing owners sharing the new owner's `householdId` plus 1 for the owner itself (not yet saved). A non-joining owner (`householdId == null`) is a sole member, so count = 1.\n\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `assignHouseholdSize` into the pipeline right after `assignHousehold` (so the `householdId` is already set) and before `assignCustomerCode`, under the request transaction.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `membershipTier` expression now returns `GOLD` when `householdMemberCount >= 3`, otherwise falls through to the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules.\n\n**How the test path works:** three owners created with the same last name + address and `sharesHousehold: true` form one household. `AssignHousehold` links them under a shared `householdId`; for the third create, `AssignHouseholdSize` counts 2 existing members + 1 = 3, persisted on save. On `GET`, the mapper sees `householdMemberCount == 3` and returns `GOLD`.",
